UseMod:InterWiki link: UseMod:InterWiki -- &lt;nowiki&gt;UseMod:InterWiki&lt;/nowiki&gt;

You can separate links from adjacent text with spaces or the special &quot;&quot; (two double-quotes) delimiter.  The &quot;&quot; delimiter is &lt;i&gt;not&lt;/i&gt; displayed--it is useful for cases like plural forms of page links (such as UseMod:UseModWiki&quot;&quot;s).  In nearly all cases trailing punctuation is ignored, so you can safely make links like http://www.usemod.com/, without the trailing comma being part of the link.
You can also use UseMod:FreeLinks.
== Lists: ==
Simple lists:
&lt;pre&gt;
* Text for a bulleted list item.
** Text for second-level list.
*** Text for third level, etc.
&lt;/pre&gt;

...which looks like:
* Text for a bulleted list item.
